# Increment Ineligibility Criteria Exclusions

The module is labelled **Increment Ineligibility Criteria** in the UI: every active row in `increment_eligibility_criteria` is a disqualification rule. Breaching any active criterion ⇒ `eligibility = 'ineligible'`, `eligible_percent = 0`. Employees who don't breach continue through PMS score → slab → method as normal.

Internal table/column names (`increment_eligibility_*`, `increment_eligibility_exclusions`) are retained for back-compat — only display labels changed (see ADR-069).

Senior employees / board members can be exempted from these ineligibility criteria via the `increment_eligibility_exclusions` table. Exemption bypasses the criteria block ONLY — PMS score, slab, increment method, salary inputs, and confirmation-increment rules still apply.

## Per-AY rule (locked)
- Each exclusion row is keyed by `(config_id, employee_id, assessment_year)` — UNIQUE constraint.
- An exclusion applies **only** to its stored `assessment_year`. Same employee in 2026-27 is fully evaluated unless a separate row exists.
- There is no "apply to all years" option. UI explicitly forbids it.

## Evaluator contract
`evaluateIncrementEligibility(metrics, criteria, validationDate, { employeeId, assessmentYear, exclusions, exclusionReasons })`
- Short-circuits to `{ eligible: true, excluded: true, exclusion_reason }` only when `exclusions.has(\`${employeeId}|${assessmentYear}\`)`.
- Use `exclusionKey(empId, ay)` helper from `useIncrementEligibility` to build the Set keys.

## UI
- `ExclusionsCard` renders inside `IncrementEligibilitySection`, after the Criteria table.
- Default view: filtered to the loaded AY. Toggle "Show all years" enters a read-only cross-AY view (Add/Remove disabled).
- Employee picker uses `useActiveEmployeesForCopy` + `EmployeeCombobox multiple`.
- Add panel requires explicit AY selection (prefilled with loaded AY). Duplicates silently skipped via `upsert({ ignoreDuplicates: true })`; toast reports `inserted` vs `skipped`.
- Remove → `ConfirmDestructiveDialog`.
- Add/Remove hidden when config status is `approved` or `archived`.

## RLS / Audit
- SELECT/INSERT/DELETE restricted to `admin` or `hr_pms`.
- Trigger `log_increment_eligibility_exclusion_change` writes `exclusion_added` / `exclusion_removed` rows to `increment_eligibility_audit` with employee snapshot in `revised_value` / `previous_value` jsonb.
